  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-03-03T16:26:17.512Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "In unity, it's very easy to add and configure new quality settings. Right now, we only have the three: \"VRHigh\", \"VRLow\", and \"DesktopLow.\"\n\nI believe it would be beneficial to the community if this were expanded greatly in both directions, especially lower.\n\nLow-end computers that are just within specs (like mine) can struggle with larger rooms, and along with steamVR's general slowness and poor low-framerate compensation, the game becomes unplayable in VR.\n\nWith the addition of lower quality levels, (perhaps including a baseline level with everything set to the minimum) many users like myself will become able to play.\n\nA \"feature\" such as this will only take a matter of minutes to add, and would make all the difference for a lot of players.",
